The Newman–Shanks–Williams prime sequence is a sequence of prime numbers of the form \(3^n - 1\). However, the sequence starts with \(3^2 - 1 = 8\), which is not a prime number. The correct primes in this sequence are \(3^3 - 1 = 7\), \(3^4 - 1 = 17\), and \(3^5 - 1 = 43\).

